.TH CRS-TUNNEL 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-tunnel \- open, close, probe or attach to the ssh tunnels for the control\-room VNC sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-tunnel
.BR open | close | status | connect
.RB [ \-\-session
.IR NAME " |"
.B \-\-host
.IR H " |"
.BR \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-ssh\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-viewer
.IR BIN ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs on the operator's machine outside the DAQ network.
For each selected session of
.I controlroom.yaml
it maintains one backgrounded master ssh,
.PP
.EX
ssh \-o GSSAPIAuthentication=yes \-o GSSAPIDelegateCredentials=yes \e
    \-J GATEWAY \-f \-N \-M \-S ~/.crs/ssh\-ctrl\-HOST\-LPORT \e
    \-o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \-L LPORT:localhost:5900+DISPLAY USER@HOST
.EE
.PP
where
.I USER
is
.B personal_user
from the configuration, or the session account when that is empty.
The forward's far end is resolved on the session host, which is the only
place the VNC server listens (it is started with
.BR "\-localhost yes" ).
The local listener has no explicit bind address, so it is loopback\-only
unless the client's ssh configuration sets
.BR GatewayPorts .
The login user on the jump host is not set by this tool; it comes from
the client's
.BR ssh_config (5)
or the local user name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open
Check for a Kerberos ticket
.RB ( "klist \-s" ),
then open each selected tunnel not already open.
The first failure aborts the remaining sessions.
.TP
.B close
.B "ssh \-O exit"
on each control socket, then remove the socket file.
.TP
.B status
One line per session: name, open or closed, local port, host, VNC port,
account.
A socket that fails
.B "ssh \-O check"
is deleted and reported closed.
Selects
.B \-\-all
when no target is given.
.TP
.B connect
Open if needed, then start a viewer on
.BR localhost: LPORT :
.B "open vnc://localhost:LPORT"
(macOS Screen Sharing) when no
.B \-\-viewer
is given on macOS, otherwise
.IB BIN " \-Shared localhost:" LPORT
with
.I BIN
defaulting to
.B vncviewer
on the PATH or the TigerVNC application bundle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-session " NAME"
one session by name.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " H"
every session on host
.I H
(short name or FQDN).
.TP
.B \-\-all
every configured session.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
.IR controlroom.yaml .
Default:
.BR $CRS_CONFIG ,
else
.I ./config/controlroom.yaml
relative to the working directory, else the copy in the package tree.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-config " FILE"
passed to ssh as
.BR \-F ;
used by the test suite.
.TP
.BI \-\-viewer " BIN"
VNC client for
.BR connect .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.crs/ssh\-ctrl\-SHORTHOST\-LPORT
one control socket per open tunnel.
.TP
.I config/controlroom.yaml
sessions, gateway,
.BR personal_user .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_CONFIG
configuration path.
.TP
.B CRS_GATEWAY
overrides
.B gateway
(the
.B \-J
host).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a configuration error, unknown session or host, no
Kerberos ticket, or a failed
.BR "ssh \-f" ;
2 on a command\-line error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
crs\-tunnel status
crs\-tunnel open \-\-all
crs\-tunnel connect \-\-session shift\-main
crs\-tunnel close \-\-host mu2e\-mgr\-01
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR crs\-gui (1),
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
